(4950114, 718971, 48697, '<td valign="top">I feel the stone background draws attention from the beautiful crystal.  I feel a simpler background would have drawn more attention to your product.</td>', 'I feel the stone background draws attention from the beautiful crystal.  I feel a simpler background would have drawn more attention to your product.', '2008-09-11 11:37:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(4950116, 718845, 9285, '<td valign="top">Watch the shadows. For a product shoot, it''ll make or break the photo. In This case, the shadow is too "artificial". Usually, for a stock photo, it''ll be good to not have shadow. But for product shots, it might be better to have some natural shadows. Other than that, the framing, composition is good. Hope this helps.</td>', 'Watch the shadows. For a product shoot, it''ll make or break the photo. In This case, the shadow is too "artificial". Usually, for a stock photo, it''ll be good to not have shadow. But for product shots, it might be better to have some natural shadows. Other than that, the framing, composition is good. Hope this helps.', '2008-09-11 11:37:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(4950133, 719077, 78132, '<td valign="top">Very clever!</td>', 'Very clever!', '2008-09-11 11:43:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(4950142, 718874, 9285, '<td valign="top">A good quality stock/ product shot. Very well controlled lighting, exposure and DOF. In those areas, it''ll be a 10/10<br/> <br/>Since this is a product shot, I would improve on 2 areas (rather minor)<br/>1) The framing - I''ll give it a little more room on both the left and right. This will improve the "usability" of the photo in magazines and catalogs. Moreover, the crop of the photo gives it a rather tight feel.<br/>2) The table line at the bottom is not "contributing". Meaning it''s not adding value to the shot. The reason you''ve put the product against a plain background is to bring out the product and make it stand out. The table line (edge) is rather distracting. I would crop it out.<br/> <br/>An overall 8 for me. A lot of technical consideration had gone into this shot!</td>', 'A good quality stock/ product shot. Very well controlled lighting, exposure and DOF. In those areas, it''ll be a 10/10 Since this is a product shot, I would improve on 2 areas (rather minor)1) The framing - I''ll give it a little more room on both the left and right. This will improve the "usability" of the photo in magazines and catalogs. Moreover, the crop of the photo gives it a rather tight feel.2) The table line at the bottom is not "contributing". Meaning it''s not adding value to the shot. The reason you''ve put the product against a plain background is to bring out the product and make it stand out. The table line (edge) is rather distracting. I would crop it out. An overall 8 for me. A lot of technical consideration had gone into this shot!', '2008-09-11 11:47:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4950197, 719077, 98428, '<td valign="top">i absolutly love this one, not just because i love rockstar... <br/>love the editing..</td>', 'i absolutly love this one, not just because i love rockstar... love the editing..', '2008-09-11 12:17:09.000000', NULL, 1),
