(4962955, 719082, 86090, '<td valign="top">**Greetings from the critic club**<br/> <br/>I think this is a nice product shot, even thoug your focus seems to be a bit off, you are showing nice detail of your product, wich is what most people like, specially if you are buying from the web or a catalogue.<br/> <br/>Technical aspects: I think you did a good job with the background, and the composition is pleasing, though some people would have prefer a different angle, maybe positioning the camera at the same level as the mugs. The lighting is acceptable, but I think you can get a cleaner picture, one without reflections, it help if you can use a softbox, and some reflecting items, sometimes even need a double diffusion.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.</td>', '**Greetings from the critic club** I think this is a nice product shot, even thoug your focus seems to be a bit off, you are showing nice detail of your product, wich is what most people like, specially if you are buying from the web or a catalogue. Technical aspects: I think you did a good job with the background, and the composition is pleasing, though some people would have prefer a different angle, maybe positioning the camera at the same level as the mugs. The lighting is acceptable, but I think you can get a cleaner picture, one without reflections, it help if you can use a softbox, and some reflecting items, sometimes even need a double diffusion. I hope this helps.', '2008-09-18 22:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963078, 717357, 47205, '<td valign="top">This is awesome Ray!!! Awesome color and comp in this. Congrats on your placement my friend. Hope you stay warm and well this coming winter...and not much snow your way :-)</td>', 'This is awesome Ray!!! Awesome color and comp in this. Congrats on your placement my friend. Hope you stay warm and well this coming winter...and not much snow your way :-)', '2008-09-19 00:24:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4963290, 719223, 25355, '<td valign="top">I did a very similar series of shots a couple of years ago when I got a new female Woody (red), but I never got around to processing and posting them. (The idea was to have a short movie sequence of still images of her emerging from the box with the other Woodies helping her out.)<br/>   You did quite well, really.</td>', 'I did a very similar series of shots a couple of years ago when I got a new female Woody (red), but I never got around to processing and posting them. (The idea was to have a short movie sequence of still images of her emerging from the box with the other Woodies helping her out.)   You did quite well, really.', '2008-09-19 02:08:41.000000', NULL, 0),
